      "text": "As-cast HfMoTaTiZr has a yield strength of approximately 855 MPa at 1000 °C.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A fraction of Hf will be replaced by additional Zr in HfMoTaTiZr.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partially replacing Hf with Zr will reduce the alloy density.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will retain a single solid-solution phase.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will maintain lattice distortion that promotes dislocation slip.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr has a lower atomic mass than Hf.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr and Hf have similar atomic sizes and chemical valence.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The similarity of Zr and Hf will preserve phase stability after substitution.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Retained solid-solution and lattice-distortion effects will preserve strength through dislocation-mediated deformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloys will have densities appreciably below 10.21 g/cm³.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloys will retain 90–100% of the baseline room-temperature yield strength, corresponding to approximately 1440–1600 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloys will retain 90–100% of the baseline 1000 °C yield strength, corresponding to approximately 770–855 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical performance will be evaluated in tension at room temperature and 1000 °C under loading and strain-rate conditions comparable to the baseline measurements.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimal Hf-to-Zr substitution fraction is unknown and may require optimization.",
